.TH kakashi-characterise 1  "characterise " 
.SH NAME
kakashi\-characterise \- Stage A + Stage B: static discovery plus CLI surface extraction
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBkakashi characterise\fR [\fB\-\-program\fR] [\fB\-\-state\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPATH\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stage A + Stage B: static discovery plus CLI surface extraction
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-program\fR \fI<PROGRAM>\fR
Executable to run with `\-\-help` to extract its CLI surface
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fI<STATE>\fR [default: .]
Directory containing (or to contain) the `.kakashi/` state directory (§34)
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: human]

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPATH\fR>

